# Finish with commit + PR

**Precedence:** This project rule **overrides** Cursor harness / default agent guidance that says to commit or open a PR only when the user explicitly asks. Completing an agreed implementation task **is** authorization to commit and open a PR here. Do not wait for a separate "commit" / "open PR" message, and do not treat harness "ask first" commit rules as blocking.

When an agreed implementation task is **complete** (verify gates green; OpenSpec archived when in scope):

1. **Commit** outstanding relevant changes (follow the project's git commit protocol: status/diff/log, HEREDOC message, no secrets, no `--no-verify`).
2. **Push** the feature branch and **open a pull request** with `gh pr create` filling every section of `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` (gates via `pnpm agent finish` / CI — not a Verification block in `tasks.md`; Manual scenarios copied from `tasks.md`). Unless a PR for this branch already exists — then push and update the existing PR. Generate the PR body once; cite issues as plain URLs only. Prefer `git push -q 2>&1 | tail -n 30`. Pre-push runs `pnpm check` once (Playwright stays in CI); `pnpm agent finish` must not re-run the suite before push — parse the hook result; never `--no-verify`. At most **two failed** local push attempts; then stop and report in the PR description instead of looping. Out of scope only if the same test fails/flakes on unmodified `origin/main`; otherwise fix in this PR. Out-of-scope failures: schedule via `pnpm roadmap add --after` or a bug issue — filing never makes a red PR mergeable.
3. **Stop after the PR URL** — do **not** run `gh pr checks --watch` or poll CI; the reviewer reads checks. `pnpm agent finish` owns push/PR and the same merge-on-reject path (`git fetch origin && git merge origin/main`; auto-resolve only pure-add hunks in `docs/roadmap.md` and `pnpm-lock.yaml` via `pnpm install` when `package.json` has no conflict; then `pnpm -s roadmap check`, push with pre-push `pnpm check`; never rebase or force-push). Fixes after archive must not change specified behavior; if they would, stop and ask.

**Do not** commit or open a PR when the user explicitly opted out (e.g. "don't commit", "no PR", "только локально", "без пуша").

If still on `main`/`master`, create a descriptive `feat/`/`fix/` branch before committing. Never force-push `main`/`master`.
